window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-429f58672a1509ea"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"kick-off-coding-tasks-from-slack\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"slack\">从 Slack 发起代码任务</h1> <p>从 Slack 讨论串委派代码库工作。</p> <p>在符合条件、由工作区共享的 Codex Cloud 环境中，于 Slack 讨论串提及 <code>@ChatGPT</code> 来请求代码库工作，然后在讨论串中审阅结果。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>Slack 讨论串中已有足够上下文、适合异步交接的任务</li> <li>需要从 Slack 开始处理问题分诊、缺陷修复或范围明确的实现工作的团队</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">起步提示词</h2> <p>从讨论串启动任务</p> <p>建议模型：<code>cloud</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@ChatGPT 请调查此讨论串中关于 [repository] 的问题。\n请对 [project or environment] 使用工作区共享的 Cloud 环境。\n实施范围最小且有效的修复，运行相关检查，并在此处报告结果。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-345f9e63361a6444\">在 Slack 中使用 ChatGPT</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">Codex Cloud 环境</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">使用方法</h2> <ol> <li>让工作区管理员按照 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/third-party/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Slack 设置指南（本地尚未收录）</a>在 Slack 中启用 ChatGPT 应用。</li> <li>如果要处理代码库任务，请确认已启用 Cloud 委派，并且某个符合条件、由工作区共享的环境已有已发布版本。Enterprise 工作区请遵循<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/environments/cloud-environments#share-within-an-enterprise-workspace\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">环境共享说明</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/environments/cloud-environments\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>。</li> <li>将起步提示词复制到已启用应用的 Slack 频道或讨论串中。提供代码库、相关上下文、约束条件和期望结果。</li> <li>完成任何连接或审批提示，然后检查结果及报告中的检查项。如界面提供“跟随查看”（Follow along），可用它查看代码任务的执行过程。</li> <li>在同一讨论串中提及 <code>@ChatGPT</code> 继续处理相关工作。使用同一账户执行的后续请求可以继续原任务；换用另一个执行账户可能会启动单独任务。要切换到其它 Cloud 环境，请开始一段新对话。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"tips\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">提示</h2> <ul> <li>如果讨论串没有提供足够信息，请先概述问题和预期行为。</li> <li>指定代码库或预期使用的工作区共享环境。Slack 工作流不包含个人 Cloud 环境。</li> <li>确认执行任务的账户具有所需的环境、代码库和服务访问权限。Slack 中的一条回复不会自动授予其他人访问代码任务的权限。</li> <li>对于大型代码库，请明确限定任务范围，并指出相关文件或文件夹。</li> <li>合并前，请审阅拟议更改，并确认报告的测试覆盖了所请求的行为。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"kick-off-coding-tasks-from-slack\">Kick off coding tasks from Slack</h1> <p>Delegate repository work from Slack threads.</p> <p>Mention <code>@ChatGPT</code> in Slack to request repository work in an eligible workspace-shared Codex Cloud environment, then review the result in the thread.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Async handoffs with enough context in the Slack thread to act on</li> <li>Teams handling issue triage, bug fixes, or scoped implementation work from Slack</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Start the task from a thread</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>cloud</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@ChatGPT investigate the issue described in this thread for [repository].\nUse the workspace-shared Cloud environment for [project or environment].\nMake the smallest useful fix, run the relevant checks, and report the result here.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-345f9e63361a6444\">Use ChatGPT in Slack</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">Codex Cloud environments</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <ol> <li>Have your workspace admin enable the ChatGPT app in Slack using the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/third-party/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Slack setup guide (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</li> <li>For repository work, confirm that Cloud delegation is enabled and an eligible workspace-shared environment has a published version. For an Enterprise workspace, follow the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/environments/cloud-environments#share-within-an-enterprise-workspace\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">environment sharing guidance</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/environments/cloud-environments\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</li> <li>Copy the starter prompt into an enabled Slack channel or thread. Include the repository, relevant context, constraints, and the result you want.</li> <li>Complete any connection or approval prompts, then review the result and reported checks. When available, use <strong>Follow along</strong> to inspect the coding task.</li> <li>Mention <code>@ChatGPT</code> in the same thread for related work. Follow-ups that use the same account to run the task can continue it; another execution account may start a separate task. Start a new conversation to use a different Cloud environment.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"tips\">Tips</h2> <ul> <li>Summarize the issue and expected behavior if the thread doesn't already provide enough context.</li> <li>Name the repository or intended workspace-shared environment. Personal Cloud environments aren't included in this Slack flow.</li> <li>Check that the account running the task has the required environment, repository, and service access. A Slack reply doesn't give everyone access to the coding task.</li> <li>Keep the request scoped and name relevant files or folders in a large codebase.</li> <li>Before merging, review proposed changes and check that the reported tests cover the requested behavior.</li> </ul>"};
